# CRLF IS LOAD-BEARING IN THIS FOLDER, AND NOTHING USED TO DECLARE IT.
#
# The working tree is CRLF and the whole verification apparatus depends on it:
# 311 harness files anchor on CRLF, either as String.fromCharCode(13) or as a
# literal \r\n, because they locate a function by searching for '\r\n' plus an
# indent. A `git show` blob comes back LF, which is why every suite normalises
# its baselines; the WORKING TREE is the side that has to already be CRLF.
#
# The repository declared none of this. It worked because one machine's
# core.autocrlf happened to produce CRLF on checkout. On a clone with different
# settings -- a Linux machine, a CI runner, or simply another laptop -- the
# checkout would be LF, every CRLF-anchored search would resolve nothing, and
# the failure mode is the quiet one: indexOf returns -1, a slice runs from the
# end, and a suite reports on a block that is not there. That is the single
# largest day-one risk in handing this folder over, and it is fixed by
# declaring the convention rather than inheriting it.
#
# eol=crlf, not `text`: `text` normalises to LF in the repository and converts
# on checkout by platform, which is exactly the platform dependence this is
# removing. These files are checked out CRLF everywhere.

*.js    text eol=crlf
*.css   text eol=crlf
*.html  text eol=crlf
*.json  text eol=crlf
*.md    text eol=crlf
*.txt   text eol=crlf
*.py    text eol=crlf
*.csv   text eol=crlf

# Binary, and must never be line-ending converted.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.zip   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary

# Shapefile components: binary, and the set travels together.
*.shp   binary
*.shx   binary
*.dbf   binary
*.sbn   binary
*.sbx   binary
*.prj   text eol=crlf
